{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"s\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"…\" expr=\"1\"/>\n  </datamodel>\n  <state id=\"s\">\n    <transition event=\"e\" target=\"f\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"f\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-placeholder.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-ecmascript-data-id-placeholder.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":16,"endLine":3,"startColumn":15,"startLine":3}}}],"message":{"markdown":"identifier `…` is not an XML NCName\n\n**Note:** SCXML IDs are XML IDs: they must start with a letter or `_` and contain only NCName characters (no spaces or colons), so references can be tokenized unambiguously. An `id` is `xsd:ID`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so leading and trailing white space is not part of it: `id=\" s \"` declares `s`\n\n**Help:** a `<data id>` is both an XML ID and an ECMAScript variable name: use ASCII letters, digits, and `_`, starting with a letter\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs","text":"identifier `…` is not an XML NCName"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":128,"start":125},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML003"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML IDs are XML IDs: they must start with a letter or `_` and contain only NCName characters (no spaces or colons), so references can be tokenized unambiguously. An `id` is `xsd:ID`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so leading and trailing white space is not part of it: `id=\" s \"` declares `s`"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: rename the identifier to a valid NCName, for example replacing spaces and colons with `_`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML003` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#IDs","id":"SCXML003","name":"SCXML003","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an identifier is not an XML NCName"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}